Z||000009||ChadMan||09-30-1999||08:52 AM||||I don't mean to get in a pi$$ing contest, DXR_WILL, but <A HREF="http://www.motortrend.com" TARGET=_blank>www.motortrend.com</A>  says:<P>"Honda's high-revving S2000 roadster has been priced at $32,000 MSRP (Manufacturer's Suggested Retail Price).<P>The S2000, which recently went on sale, was developed to celebrate Honda's 50th anniversary and as a reflection of the company's racing spirit. Its 2.0-liter/240-horsepower engine boasts more horsepower per liter an any normally aspirated production car currently available. It is also the first car in its class to earn a low emission vehicle (LEV) rating."<P>That's pretty cheap for what this car will do.  Still, just think of the Fiero you could build for $20K, let alone $32K.<P><BR>||||reg||1
